## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of data protection basics in Snowflake using masking policies and role-based access. It also covers applying policies, privilege grants, and simple auditing.

## Key Concepts
- Dynamic data masking with MASKING POLICY
- CURRENT_ROLE() for access decisions
- GRANT/REVOKE science for roles
- Auditing access via QA tables

## Code Example
```javascript
CREATE MASKING POLICY budget_masking AS (val NUMBER) RETURNS NUMBER ->
CASE WHEN (CURRENT_ROLE() IN ('FINANCE_ROLE')) THEN val ELSE 0 END;

ALTER TABLE PUBLIC.PROJECT_BUDGET MODIFY COLUMN budget SET MASKING POLICY budget_masking;

CREATE ROLE FINANCE_ROLE;
CREATE ROLE ANALYST_ROLE;
GRANT USAGE ON DATABASE <DB> TO ROLE ANALYST_ROLE;
GRANT SELECT ON PUBLIC.PROJECT_BUDGET TO ROLE ANALYST_ROLE;
GRANT USAGE ON DATABASE <DB> TO ROLE FINANCE_ROLE;
GRANT SELECT ON PUBLIC.PROJECT_BUDGET TO ROLE FINANCE_ROLE;
```

